  "narrative": "WellMail malware WellMail is a lightweight tool designed to run commands or scripts with the results being sent to a hardcoded Command and Control (C2) server. Persistent access Upon gaining access to a system, the group likely drops further tooling and/or seeks to obtain legitimate credentials to the compromised systems in order to maintain persistent access. WellMess is a lightweight malware designed to execute arbitrary shell commands, upload and download files.",
